    <mj-section background-color="#eff1f4" padding="1px 1px 1px 1px" border-radius="10px">
  <mj-column background-color="#fff" border-radius="10px" padding="0px">
    <mj-image
      border-radius="10px 10px 0 0"
      padding="0"
      width="600px"
      src="https://www.londonsummary.com/email/images/REPLACE_ME.jpg"
      alt="Reform roadmap rolls"
      href="https://www.londonsummary.com/"
    />
    <mj-text
      padding="20px 20px 0px 20px"
      font-family="Austin News Text Web, TNYAdobeCaslonPro, 'Times New Roman', serif"
      color="#000000"
    >
      <h2 style="font-size: 24px; line-height: 1.2; font-weight: 400; margin: 0;">
        Reform roadmap rolls
      </h2>
    </mj-text>
    <mj-text padding="0px 20px 0px 20px" font-family="Arial" color="#000000">
      <p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>What’s happening?</strong> Keir Starmer has set out the <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/politics/2026/may/13/kings-speech-government-keir-starmer-legislative-agenda-next-12-months" target="_blank" style="text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 2px solid #80011F; color: black;">UK government’s agenda for the next year</a> through the King’s Speech. The plan includes major bills on public services, housing, immigration, the economy, and Europe. The government also wants closer alignment with the EU, faster innovation rules, tougher measures on late payments, and housing protections.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 1.5; padding-top: 15px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>Details:</strong> Plans include closer UK-EU cooperation, full nationalisation of British Steel, faster innovation rules, and tougher penalties for late-paying firms. Public service changes include abolishing NHS England, reforming special educational needs, and limiting some jury trials. Housing reforms target leaseholds, right-to-buy rules, and unsafe cladding, while immigration proposals would tighten asylum and refugee protections.
</p>
<p style="font-size: 16px; line-height: 24px; padding-top: 15px; padding-bottom: 20px; margin: 0;">
  <strong>What’s missing? </strong>The King’s Speech did not include a standalone welfare reform bill, despite earlier expectations that the government might return to the issue. Instead, ministers said they would respond to the Milburn review and the Timms review, which are expected later this summer and autumn. The speech said that the government would continue to reform welfare to help young and disabled people flourish in work.
</p>
    </mj-text>
  </mj-column>
</mj-section>
<mj-spacer height="20px" />
